  "worked_solution": "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}\u2061x+{sin}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}\u2061x+{sin}^{2}\u2061x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{cos}^{2}\u2061x+{sin}^{2}\u2061x & ={cos}^{2}\u2061x+({sin}^{2}\u2061x+{cos}^{2}\u2061x) \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}\u2061x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}\u2061x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x=2{cos}^{2}\u2061x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x+1).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }({cos}^{2}\u2061x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }[\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x+1)+1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x+3x)|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612\\pi +3\\pi )-(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-\\pi )-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3\\pi +\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{9\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
